WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:06.800
meez... meez... meez-ahn-plahs

2
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.460
Everything... in its place.

3
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:21.400
Put your hands up if your shell just works!

4
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.100
CI's red at three a.m.

5
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.750
Pinned it once, it drifted again

6
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.040
Now the lockfile holds the line

7
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.130
Laptop, CI, same every time

8
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.900
Hooked my shell, I cd with ease

9
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.240
Everything in its place... mise

10
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.410
Give me one file, give me ease

11
00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.540
Give me one command, give me mise

12
00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.430
One file! (One file!)

13
00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:11.090
One command! (One command!)

14
00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.030
When I say MISE, you say RUN!

15
00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:13.970
MISE! (RUN!)

16
00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.300
MISE! (RUN!)

17
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:20.800
FIFTY THOUSAND TERMINALS IN THE AIR!

18
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.480
Say...

19
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.400
MISE RUN!

20
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.950
MISE RUN!

21
00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.800
meez-meez-meez-meez

22
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:56.600
MISE RUN!

23
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:06.400
MISE! (RUN!)

24
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:11.610
MISE! (RUN!)

25
00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.150
Who pinned Node? (mise use!)

26
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.990
New hire Monday? (mise install!)

27
00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.790
Who runs the tests? (mise run test!)

28
00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.690
Where's the config? (mise dot toml!)

29
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.770
nvm? (Gone!)

30
00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.170
pyenv, rbenv? (Gone!)

31
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.770
Makefile, direnv? (Gone! Gone! Gone!)

32
00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.000
One tool! (MISE!)

33
00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.970
Before the doors open

34
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.750
Before the heat

35
00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.850
Every blade laid out

36
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.050
And my heart on the beat

37
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.640
Let the whole world rush

38
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.030
I'll be standing at ease

39
00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.210
Everything in its place

40
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:56.520
'Cause I've got my mise

41
00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.240
Somewhere out there, they're rebuilding the world... just to boil water.

42
00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.760
Your flake's still flaking (flake!)

43
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.820
Your store's forty gigs (gigs!)

44
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.760
Still "experimental" (what?)

45
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.380
Year after year (year!)

46
00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.600
error: infinite recursion encountered

47
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.040
You spent the weekend configuring (config!)

48
00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.120
We spent it shipping (ship!)

49
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.100
Ship! Ship! Ship! Ship!

50
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:28.200
MISE IS NIX FOR PEOPLE WITH WORK TO DO!

51
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.900
...so get to work.

52
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:45.650
MISE RUN!

53
00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.550
MISE RUN!

54
00:03:49.550 --> 00:04:00.100
mee-mee-mee-MEEZ!

55
00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:13.400
MISE RUN!

56
00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.050
Every-thing in its place!

57
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.450
MISE! (RUN!)

58
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.900
MISE! (RUN!)

59
00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:27.000
Let me hear you, people with work to do!

60
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:40.200
MISE RUN!

61
00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.790
Everything in its place

62
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.190
Everything in its place

63
00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:54.300
I've got my mise

64
00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:00.100
...exit code zero.
